 "intro": "The phase slab has put a dark fringe on the target, so a coherent packet can never reach it. But a detector that asks 'is the particle in this beam?' reveals which slit it took, and which-path information destroys interference. Place the detector over one beam after the slits, and fire it (key 1). Either answer collapses the packet into a single beam that no longer cancels at the target.",
